{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1790891502752,"sessionID":"ses_f068cf8d7fferXehlA08pIzVgk","part":{"id":"prt_0f973ac970017HEQjIbJh7x9g1","messageID":"msg_0f97398a8001G50dgg1qc7EDUl","sessionID":"ses_f068cf8d7fferXehlA08pIzVgk","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1790891565321,"sessionID":"ses_f068cf8d7fferXehlA08pIzVgk","part":{"id":"prt_0f974791c001YyeJjnXigKDhCq","messageID":"msg_0f97398a8001G50dgg1qc7EDUl","sessionID":"ses_f068cf8d7fferXehlA08pIzVgk","type":"text","text":"I have all the source needed from `src/cachetools/__init__.py` (cachetools repository):\n\n1. **Membership at the deadline**: `TTLCache.__contains__` returns `self.timer() < link.expires`. At exactly `link.expires` this is `False`, so the entry is no longer visible (strict `<` comparison; items expire when `now >= expires`).\n2. **Expired read vs. storage**: `__getitem__` detects expiry via `not (self.timer() < link.expires)` and delegates to `self.__missing__(key)`, which is `Cache.__missing__` and simply `raise KeyError(key)`. Nothing calls `Cache.__delitem__`, so the value physically stays in `__data`/`__links` until an `expire()` pass is triggered by some other operation.\n3. **Assignment refresh**: `__setitem__` freezes time via `with self.timer as time`, stores via `cache_setitem`, then (found link → `link.unlink()`) resets `link.expires = time + self.__ttl`, so an existing live entry gets a fresh deadline.\n4. **expire() reporting**: the docstring says it returns the expired `(key, value)` pairs, and the loop does `expired.append((curr.key, cache_getitem(self, curr.key)))` before `cache_delitem(self, curr.key)`, returning the list.\n\nThe default timer is `time.monotonic`, matching the monotonic-timer scenario.","time":{"start":1790891555100,"end":1790891565320}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790891565329,"sessionID":"ses_f068cf8d7fferXehlA08pIzVgk","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"rehearsal_submit_answer","callID":"call_44dd94089e7649ae973e18d0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"answer":{"assignment_refreshes_deadline":{"citations":[{"path":"src/cachetools/__init__.py","quote":"    def __setitem__(self, key, value, cache_setitem=Cache.__setitem__):\n        with self.timer as time:\n            self.expire(time)\n            cache_setitem(self, key, value)"},{"path":"src/cachetools/__init__.py","quote":"        else:\n            link.unlink()\n        link.expires = time + self.__ttl"}],"value":true},"expire_reports_removed_pairs":{"citations":[{"path":"src/cachetools/__init__.py","quote":"    def expire(self, time=None):\n        \"\"\"Remove expired items from the cache and return an iterable of the\n        expired `(key, value)` pairs.\n\n        \"\"\""},{"path":"src/cachetools/__init__.py","quote":"        while curr is not root and not (time < curr.expires):\n            expired.append((curr.key, cache_getitem(self, curr.key)))\n            cache_delitem(self, curr.key)\n            del links[curr.key]"}],"value":true},"expired_read_removes_storage":{"citations":[{"path":"src/cachetools/__init__.py","quote":"        if expired:\n            return self.__missing__(key)\n        else:\n            return cache_getitem(self, key)"},{"path":"src/cachetools/__init__.py","quote":"    def __missing__(self, key):\n        raise KeyError(key)"},{"path":"src/cachetools/__init__.py","quote":"    def __delitem__(self, key):\n        size = self.__size.pop(key)\n        del self.__data[key]\n        self.__currsize -= size"}],"value":false},"visible_at_deadline":{"citations":[{"path":"src/cachetools/__init__.py","quote":"    def __contains__(self, key):\n        try:\n            link = self.__links[key]  # no reordering\n        except KeyError:\n            return False\n        else:\n            return self.timer() < link.expires"},{"path":"src/cachetools/__init__.py","quote":"    def __init__(self, maxsize, ttl, timer=time.monotonic, getsizeof=None):"}],"value":false}}},"output":"{\"submitted\":true}","metadata":{"truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1790891565319,"end":1790891565322}},"id":"prt_0f974a104001TKKPs6lDBnMv6V","sessionID":"ses_f068cf8d7fferXehlA08pIzVgk","messageID":"msg_0f97398a8001G50dgg1qc7EDUl"}}
