{"type":"text","timestamp":1790891572779,"sessionID":"ses_f068cf8d7fferXehlA08pIzVgk","part":{"id":"prt_0f974b680001pLOCopGxbuOnA1","messageID":"msg_0f974a10e0011YigLlV5W4jJ7t","sessionID":"ses_f068cf8d7fferXehlA08pIzVgk","type":"text","text":"Answer submitted. Summary of the TTLCache behavior established from `src/cachetools/__init__.py`:\n\n- **visible_at_deadline: false** — `__contains__` uses a strict `self.timer() < link.expires` check, so at exactly the expiration time the entry is already treated as expired and invisible to membership.\n- **expired_read_removes_storage: false** — an expired `__getitem__` calls `__missing__`, which only raises `KeyError`; the stale value remains physically stored until an `expire()` pass (triggered by other operations like `__setitem__`, `__len__`, `__repr__`, or `popitem`).\n- **assignment_refreshes_deadline: true** — `__setitem__` freezes time and re-sets `link.expires = time + self.__ttl` for existing entries, giving them a fresh TTL window.\n- **expire_reports_removed_pairs: true** — `expire()` collects and returns the expired `(key, value)` pairs as it deletes them.","time":{"start":1790891570816,"end":1790891572753}}}
